content.thinking:
Interesting: some traversal requests never reach the route — Starlette router itself 404s (e.g., "../../etc/passwd" contains "/" so the path param doesn't match → default {"detail": "Not Found"}). Also ".." case? "/download/.." — httpx may normalize URL, removing it → path "/download" → 404 detail. So these are 404s from routing before any handler — filesystem untouched, but body shape differs.

Two options: add a catch-all exception... better: add a custom 404 handler for HTTPException/Starlette HTTPException to return the error envelope. That makes all 404s consistent: override StarletteHTTPException handler.

Add:

```python
from starlette.exceptions import HTTPException as StarletteHTTPException

@app.exception_handler(StarletteHTTPException)
async def http_exc_handler(request, exc):
    if exc.status_code == 404:
        return JSONResponse(404, {"error":{"code":"not_found"}})
    return JSONResponse(exc.status_code, {"error": {"detail": str(exc.detail)}})

